"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, slime_rancher.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. MelonLoader will then be installed into the game's core folder. The  required folder and .dll will be installed inside the 'Mods' folder and the UserLibs folder will be created with all its content.\nOnly the Mods and the UserLibs folder will be created automatically, the other ones will be created after starting the game.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"Slime Rancher is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'slime_rancher.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, go into Options and it should open in the 'Archipelago' tab.\n\nIn the 'Address:Port' field, enter archipelago.gg: followed by the port. This is a 5-digit number that you can find on the website after creating a new room.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nIn 'Slot name', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nFinally, click 'ARCHIPELAGO CONNECT' and then you can start playing!\n\nYou can also change some options on this tab.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for Slime Rancher Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear MelonLoader' option it will delete everything related to MelonLoader and mods. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.",
